    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Reversible six-reaction O2 variant inferred from the deposited model curves of Fig. 10a-c of the article: <strong>Selective oxidation of 3-hydroxypropionic acid to malonic acid over Pd/C: Mechanistic and kinetic study.</strong> Kim S.Y., Chavarrio J., Install J., Huber G.W. <i>Appl. Catal. B: Environ. Energy</i> 386 (2026) 126403. DOI: <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126403">10.1016/j.apcatb.2026.126403</a></p>
        <p>A reproduction aid, not a model of the paper: the text treats all reactions as irreversible and neither posted script contains this structure. It is the Table 3 O2 network with reactions 1, 2, 5 and 6 reversible; the reverse of reaction 1 is bilinear in OPA and the water formed by reactions 1 and 4. It reproduces the model curves the authors deposited for 25, 75 and 100 C (Dryad, DOI 10.5061/dryad.jsxksn0q4, files 11-1, 11-2, 11-3). </p>
        <p>Conditions: 60 mM 3-HP, 0.2 g 10 % Pd/C, NaOH/3-HP = 1:1, 3 bar O2 (Fig. 10 caption). Default state: the constants of the 75 C curve (Fig. 10b). The constants are effective first-order constants in 1/min for the 0.2 g batch, fitted separately at each temperature (25, 75 and 100 C), with no temperature law; there is no set for 50 C. All were inferred from the deposited curves and none is printed in the paper or its deposit. </p>
      </body>
    </notes>
